    <item rdf:about="https://alephnull.org/w/recipes/farro_with_mushrooms?rev=1633637056&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2021-10-07T16:04:16-0400</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>Anonymous (anonymous@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>recipes:farro_with_mushrooms</title>
        <link>https://alephnull.org/w/recipes/farro_with_mushrooms?rev=1633637056&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Farro with Mushrooms By: Martha Rose Shulman (NYT)

YIELD: 6 servings

Farro is chewier than Italian rice and doesn’t release starch when it’s cooked, so there’s no need to stir it the way you’d stir a risotto. This hearty dish has a rich, earthy flavor. Although it takes about twice as long as a risotto to cook, it doesn’t require tending.</description>
    </item>
